WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:10.072
JackedIN 1.2 is here: one terminal for SSH, Telnet, and serial, now built for automation.

2
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:24.230
Switching is easy. Import your saved sessions from PuTTY, SecureCRT, MobaXterm, or your SSH config.

3
00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:35.661
Fleet runs one command across your whole device list. Dry run shows the plan first, and passwords stay in the credential store.

4
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:48.009
Changes are verified. Exec waits for every prompt and checks an expect rule, and change prints the commit-confirm and rollback steps.

5
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:58.260
Backup pulls the running config from Cisco IOS and Juniper Junos, and diff shows exactly what changed.

6
00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:06.273
NetBox and Nautobot sync, and password-manager logins, are included at no extra charge.

7
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:15.821
An MCP server lets AI assistants use JackedIN as a tool, and an Ansible collection comes in the box.

8
00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:22.871
It runs on Windows, Linux, and Raspberry Pi. There's no Mac build yet.

9
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:29.215
Try every feature free for 72 hours. No license key needed.

10
00:01:29.565 --> 00:01:37.925
Then it's $19, one time, with a year of updates. One license, one computer.

11
00:01:38.274 --> 00:01:43.081
Get JackedIN at getpathprobe.com/jackedin.
